solution.p:
Direction cosine angles are equal to the inverse cosine of each Cartesian force component divided by the force magnitude.


    \theta_x \amp = \cos^{-1} \left(\frac{F_x}{|\vec{F}|}\right) = \cos^{-1}\left( \frac{20}{70}\right) = \ang{73.4}


    \theta_y \amp = \cos^{-1} \left(\frac{F_y}{|\vec{F}|}\right) = \cos^{-1}\left( \frac{-30}{70} \right) = \ang{115.38}


    \theta_z \amp = \cos^{-1} \left(\frac{F_z}{|\vec{F}|}\right) = \cos^{-1}\left( \frac{60}{70} \right) = \ang{31.0}

