solution.p:
The polar angle \phi is measured down from the +z axis to the vector \vec{F}.
            We can find it using a right triangle with sides F, F_z, and F_{xy}.
            Note that \phi is the same as the direction cosine angle \theta_z. \phi = \theta_z =\cos^{-1} \frac{F_z}{|\vec{F}|} = \cos^{-1}\left( \frac{60}{70} \right) = \ang{31.0}

