subsection.p:
A second application of the dot product is to find the angle between two vectors. Equation provides the procedure.
\vec{A} \cdot \vec{B} \amp = | \vec{A} | | \vec{B} |\cos \theta
\cos \theta \amp = \frac{\vec{A} \cdot \vec{B}}{ | \vec{A} | | \vec{B} |}

solution.p:


    \cos \theta \amp = \frac{\ihat \cdot \jhat}{ | \ihat | | \jhat |}


    \amp = \frac{(1)(0) + (0)(1) + (0)(0)}{(1)(1)}


    \amp = 0



    \theta \amp = \cos^{-1}(0)


    \amp = \ang{90}


This shows that \ihat and \jhat are perpendicular to each other.

